 "final_passage": "On the Merriwold-Dialog 2.0 test set, Corvane-DST achieved a higher mean joint goal accuracy (JGA) than Halloway-DST (56.8% vs 56.1%), although no statistical test was reported for this comparison. Corvane-DST significantly outperformed the Pipkin-Span baseline on the same test set (mean difference 4.5 percentage points, 95% CI [3.51, 5.5], p < 0.001). On the Tarnby-Schema test set with services unseen in training, Corvane-DST also significantly exceeded Halloway-DST in JGA (mean difference 2.3 percentage points, 95% CI [1.18, 3.42], p = 0.0046). Per-domain results on single-domain Merriwold-Dialog 2.0 test dialogues were mixed, with Corvane-DST higher in train, restaurant, and attraction but lower in hotel and taxi than Halloway-DST, and an ablation indicated that both slot descriptions and history compression contribute to Corvane-DST's JGA (56.8% full vs 54.9% without descriptions, 55.7% without compression, and 53.6% without both).",
